+# Engineering20 local verification scope
+
+Authorization: BRAIN-ONSKIN-AUTONOMOUS-PRODUCT-COMPLETION-20 / ENGINEERING20_DEFENSIVE_001. Source work stays on the existing Windows worktree and branch. All 38 requirements and 18 gates remain formally UNACCEPTED; release NO_GO.
+
+The phase-specific evidence directory is the sibling `../ENGINEERING20_EVIDENCE/`. Final receipts, exact source identities, diagnostic failures and packaging hashes are recorded there; this document does not substitute for those receipts.
+
+Consumer human-simulated E2E ran against actual local Expo web in isolated Edge with providers blocked, offline Metro and an explicitly synthetic owner. At both 375x667 and 430x932 it entered adult DOB and consent through the UI, created a manual bottle, explicitly saved an encrypted unconfirmed transcription, reloaded, resumed and reviewed the saved source, confirmed the observation, reloaded again, and reviewed/canceled/confirmed draft discard. A second same-origin tab refused access before private app storage reads; after closing the first tab it explicitly retried and resumed. Screenshots and DOM/geometry/network receipts are retained in `bottle-browser-r4/`. Keyboard activation and 44px minimum targets were checked for principal save/confirm/retry/discard controls; captured screens had no horizontal overflow.
+
+Professional E2E ran the actual local Vite UI at both viewports. The real API returned 503. Explicitly synthetic HTTP responses exercised current source review, cancellation, exact retry, queue transition, no owner response then decline linked to an exact intended version, closure with recorded nonacknowledgement reason, history, filters, keyboard/focus, read-only and unavailable states. These fixtures are not authentication, licensing, delivery, custody, payment or production authority. Receipts and screenshots are in `professional-browser/`.
+
+The initial consumer browser attempts exposed harness/environment issues: restricted localhost access, an obsolete category control name, and an incomplete Shelf accessibility label. The harness was corrected to use observed controls. No app acceptance was claimed from failed attempts. An initial mounted-flow regression in navigation discard during source review was fixed by permitting the explicit leaving decision, while retaining stale-decision fences; the original test then passed. Type errors and unsupported Turbo flag combinations are retained as engineering diagnostics. The first concurrent full-suite attempt hit an existing 5-second professional history test timeout under simultaneous build/check load; the complete suite is rerun without that competing load, with no timeout or assertion weakened.
+
+Additional ordinary source tests exercise actual encryption/readback, stable identity and exact CAS, source changes, current adult/owner/consent/epoch authority, omitted writes, missing keys, unknown formats, delayed callbacks, paused-processing rights export, foreign-owner refusal, authorized withdrawal failure/retry, and drain-before-erasure. Existing photo/recovery tests remain intact.
+
+The complete suite also caught older fixtures that assumed one bottle-history query, no native platform import in auth storage, an exact React import list, and that every `layerwell.*` literal named persisted storage. Fixtures now admit the real Web Lock, represent the separate draft query, and classify the lock name as non-storage; all prior behavioral assertions remain. The professional projection accepts the existing receipt domain's finite nonnegative timestamps, including zero/fractional values, with the JavaScript date upper bound enforced.
+
+Uncovered qualifications remain open: native/physical device persistence and accessibility, genuine OCR/camera providers, process or OS crash durability, multiple native processes, older ungated browser builds, real accounts/backend custody, professional staff/licence/payment authority, clinical/scientific/device evidence, independent security and release acceptance. Manual intake and optional correction drafts still have their prior memory-only behavior. Explicit bottle saves retain only the latest successful save; later unsaved edits can be lost on restart. No external service or native attempt was run.
